# A thread wake-up starts a turn the user did not ask for. When it ends, the phone
# hears nothing: a watched issue with a comment every few minutes would otherwise ring
# for every one. A turn the user starts still notifies, so the channel is not silenced,
# only the turns CST itself began.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_gh
fake_telegram private
session app Watched session
watch_thread https://github.com/o/r/discussions/7
held_reply https://github.com/o/r/discussions/7

wait_for Watched session
press enter
# Opening the session delivers the held wake-up; the stub acts it out as a 3 s turn.
wait_for Fake Copilot received: A new comment arrived on
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Watched session
# The wake-up turn ends while we are away. Its text exists, but no notification
# carries it: nobody at the keyboard started that turn.
wait 5000
telegram_expect_not Handled the comment
telegram_expect_not Ready for attention
telegram_dump 01-quiet-after-wake
dump 01-list-after-wake

# A turn the user starts ends loud, as before.
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
type e2e:work 1500 Finished what you asked for.
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Watched session
telegram_wait Finished what you asked for.
telegram_dump 02-user-turn-notifies
dump 02-list-after-user-turn
